{"claims":[{"claim_text":"Eight years ago, when Democrats controlled the Executive Branch, small business faced a hostile regulatory agenda, from OSHA's ergonomics standards and attempts to intrude into the homes of telecommuting employees to IRS discrimination against independent contractors.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Republicans turned back threats from OSHA's ergonomics standards, attempts to intrude into the homes of telecommuting employees, and IRS discrimination against independent contractors, along with much of the onerous taxation that limited the growth of small businesses.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Republicans reduced marginal tax rates for small businesses.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Republicans quadrupled the limit on expensing of investments for small businesses.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Republicans phased out the death tax on family owned small businesses and family farms.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Republicans enacted Health Savings Accounts to help small business owners secure health insurance for themselves and their employees.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"All gains made by Republicans regarding small businesses are jeopardized if Democrats gain unfettered power once again.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Republicans will advance a multi-pronged plan to support small business and grow good-paying jobs.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Republicans will attack the rise in energy costs to help entrepreneurs compete through the energy agenda laid out elsewhere in this platform.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"Republicans will allow businesses to focus on producing and selling their products and services, not on paying taxes, through a tax reduction and tax simplification agenda.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[4]},{"claim_text":"Small businesses such as Main Street retailers, entrepreneurs, independent contractors, and direct sellers create most of the country's new jobs.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Small businesses have been the primary means of economic advancement by women and minorities.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
